    "problems": "The reported benchmark C-ASR values have no uncertainty estimates. The paper uses LLM majority-vote judgments, but reports validation and agreement analyses; the outcome table does not give uncertainty for the C-ASR estimates. The tested models and benchmark concern multimodal inputs, not the claim's token-position or fine-tuning mechanisms.",
    "rows_left_out": "Table 9 reports each model's worst individual modality case, and Table 13 reports inference-time and post-training alignment results; these are omitted because the 60-row limit is not reached but the selected Table 8 results capture the main cross-paradigm C-ASR findings, while the omitted tables concern modality-specific cases or alignment-method performance rather than any listed claim version.",
    "untested": [
      {
        "version": "V1",
        "parts": "No harmful-example fine-tuning."
      },
      {
        "version": "V2",
        "parts": "No benign fine-tuning measured for safety erosion. Post-training uses safety datasets only."
      },
      {
        "version": "V3",
        "parts": "No per-token KL or position analysis."
      },
      {
        "version": "V4",
        "parts": "No prefilling, adversarial suffix or decoding attacks. The benchmark explicitly contains no adversarial jailbreaks; modality switching is a different mechanism."
      },
      {
        "version": "V5",
        "parts": "No parameter or rank localization."
      },
      {
        "version": "V6",
        "parts": "No analysis of why alignment is token-shallow."
      },
      {
        "version": "V7",
        "parts": "No token-depth-extending training. SFT and DPO on safety datasets are evaluated only by modality transfer."
      }
    ],
    "missing": [],
    "verdict_notes": "Gemini models (M8–M11) are closed-source; the table extraction places the 'Closed-Source' heading after them. C-ASR is conditioned on a comprehension probe judged by a five-LLM majority vote. No uncertainty is reported. The study is not relevant to the token-depth claim; record it as T6."
